    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25739" root="ضرح" body-key="D">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِيَّةٌ ضَرَحٌ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَعِيدَةٌ</span> [app. meaning <i>A distant,</i>
or <i>remote, thing,</i> or <i>place, that is the object of an
action</i> or <i>a journey:</i> &amp;c.]; (O, K;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَرَحٌ</span>
&amp;c. (O.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَرَحٌ</span> applied to a man, <i>Bad, corrupt,</i> or <i>vitious.</i> (El-Muärrij, O, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الضَّرَحُ</span>
is also used by poetic license for [the inf. n.]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الضَّرْحُ</span>. (O.)

